WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.370
Mario has always smashed blocks; now he's
also smashing the box office.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:10.000
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" had the biggest
opening weekend of 2023 so far, and there

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.010
are lots of reasons why.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:17.369
The "Super Mario Bros." franchise began way
back in the medium's infancy, with the 1981

00:00:17.369 --> 00:00:18.920
arcade release "Donkey Kong."

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.160
It officially blew up in popularity with the
worldwide release of the Nintendo Entertainment

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.390
System, known in Japan as the Famicom, in
the mid-'80s.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:31.030
Even then, critics were sure that "Super Mario
Bros." would be an international phenomenon.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:35.090
Mario has remained a staple of Nintendo's
carefully curated brand ever since.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.500
The series has spawned countless spin-offs,
from "Mario Kart" to "Mario Party."

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.760
Some of these side projects rank among the
best-selling video game franchises of all

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.710
time, apart from the broader Mario umbrella
that is.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:51.820
More than 800 million Mario video game units
have been sold, with the series' most recent

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:57.079
entry, "Super Mario 3D World + Bowser's Fury"
on Nintendo Switch, selling just under 10

00:00:57.079 --> 00:00:59.120
million units in 2021.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:04.080
The series has been prime material for adaptation
into an animated film for a very long time.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.480
Its colorful aesthetics, unique world, and
lovable cast of characters not only appeal

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.080
to kids, but to nostalgic adults who grew
up with the franchise's earlier entries.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.177
It's no surprise that the series' video game
success has translated to its box office win.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:22.810
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" isn't Nintendo's
first brush with translating their most beloved

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.400
franchise to film.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.910
In 1993, the live-action "Super Mario Bros."
movie starred Bob Hoskins and John Leguizamo

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.100
as Mario and Luigi, respectively.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.000
Similar to the Illumination movie, the film
follows the two blue-collar brothers working

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.060
as plumbers in Brooklyn before they're sent
through an interdimensional portal to another

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.070
world inhabited by a kingdom of dinosaurs.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.790
But things get pretty different from there.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:48.560
Notably, the film was a critical failure and
bombed at the box office.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.220
The New York Times said that the film's final
30 minutes were nearly unwatchable and criticized

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.979
its inability to capture the magic of the
original games.

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:00.281
"Super Mario Bros." was even hated by the
cast, with Hoskins naming the film as one

00:02:00.281 --> 00:02:01.490
of his biggest regrets.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.470
That said, Leguizamo has embraced it in recent
years.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.480
"I knew you had been in the Super Mario Bros.
movie."

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.480
"Shh!"

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.480
"With, but, with uh…"

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.245
"No, I'm proud of it.

00:02:10.245 --> 00:02:12.050
I'm proud of it now."

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.370
The 30-year-old film has developed something
of a cult audience, though.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:19.280
Directors Rocky Morton and Annabel Jankel
told Variety that midnight screenings held

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.818
at Quentin Tarantino's New Beverly Cinema
helped them feel proud of the work they'd done.

00:02:23.818 --> 00:02:27.835
Though Morton admitted that it might have
turned out differently if Nintendo was more involved.

00:02:27.835 --> 00:02:31.930
Nevertheless, hardcore "Super Mario Bros."
fans were optimistic about Illumination's

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.920
chances given that Nintendo is very careful
with its IP nowadays, with many of them excited

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.227
enough to see the film in theaters.

00:02:39.227 --> 00:02:43.530
There are lots of adults who grew up playing
titles such as "Super Mario World" and "Super

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.000
Mario 64."

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.590
Although Illumination's more original projects,
like the "Despicable Me" films or "Sing,"

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.840
may largely appeal to kids, there's a whole
generation of grown-ups who were curious to

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.450
see their favorite childhood games get referenced
in "The Super Mario Bros. Movie."

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.030
Critics seem to be noting the film's dedication
to appealing to the franchise's longtime fans.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.909
They've noted that the movie is focused on
channeling nostalgia for the games while also

00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:09.110
opening up the world to new audiences.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.810
This is arguably a strength that Illumination
has lacked with their previous adaptations

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.780
of Dr. Seuss's story books.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.629
Both "The Grinch" and "The Lorax" were criticized
for their lack of faithfulness to the source material.

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:23.330
Thankfully, faithfulness is the name of the
game in "The Super Mario Bros. Movie."

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:28.310
The film's visuals beautifully recapture the
aesthetics of recent "Mario" video game titles.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:33.269
It's also quite the far cry from the 1993
film, which took quite a few major creative

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:37.470
liberties with the design of characters including
Bowser and Toad.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.911
Illumination's film remains true to the characters
that video game fans have come to know and love.

00:03:41.911 --> 00:03:46.120
Even though Illumination has been criticized
at times, they've never failed to release

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.209
a film that does well commercially.

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:53.180
The studio debuted in 2010 with the original
"Despicable Me," which introduced audiences

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.690
to the Minions, who are either adorable or
annoying, depending on who you ask.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:04:01.750
They've become the company's mascots, and
the spinoff film "Minions" ranks in the top

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.430
30 highest-grossing films of all time.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.870
Most of the company's success has been attributed
to their low-cost production, with Illumination

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.980
CEO Chris Meledandri listing off their secrets
to The New York Times:

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.370
"Very few management layers, clear decision-making,
shortening the length of time you spend developing

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.690
a movie — it can be done."

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.720
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" does its utmost
to appeal to not only fans of the series'

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.340
more recent entries, but longtime followers
from the arcade days.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.250
Whether it's through iconic '80s needle drops,
memorable enemies from the franchise, or broader

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:38.160
meta references to the series' history, "The
Super Mario Bros. Movie" is a blast for anyone

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.160
who grew up playing "Mario" games.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.600
Some critics have actually knocked the movie
for emphasizing references and visual fidelity

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.950
to the games over plot, character development,
and themes, comparing it unfavorably to other

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.139
game-centric films like "Wreck-It Ralph."

00:04:52.139 --> 00:04:53.139
"It's grown-up stuff.

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:54.470
You wouldn't understand."

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:58.850
That said, no "Super Mario Bros." game has
ever really been acclaimed for its story,

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:03.780
aside from maybe RPG titles such as "Paper
Mario: The Thousand Year Door" or "Mario and

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.509
Luigi: Superstar Saga."

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:09.950
Many of those who care enough to see Mario
and his friends translated to the screen likely

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.620
won't mind a paper-thin story, so to speak.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.695
The appeal of the games has always been visuals
and action, and the movie has those to spare.

00:05:17.695 --> 00:05:22.460
Sequences like Mario and Luigi's early scenes
in Brooklyn or Mario's introduction to the

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.759
marketplace of the Mushroom Kingdom are chock
full of references and Easter eggs.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:31.760
And they're not just nods to Mario's own series
of games, but also Nintendo's other properties.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:37.139
For instance, one scene in Mario's bedroom
features references to "Star Fox," "F-Zero,"

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:39.540
and "Kid Icarus" in the span of a few minutes.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.699
The movie likewise pokes fun at some tropes
of the "Super Mario Bros." franchise.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:48.090
As Mario and Toad try to sneak into Peach's
castle, they're stopped by two Toad guards

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.690
who smugly tell them, "the princess is in
another castle," a line players of the original

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:54.660
NES game will surely recognize.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:59.069
Every viewing of "The Super Mario Bros. Movie"
is likely to result in spotting a background

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:03.539
cameo, callback, or visual flourish that will
excite anyone who's familiar with the "Super

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:04.949
Mario Bros." series.

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:09.820
For gamers who love getting 100% completion
in the games they play, "The Super Mario Bros.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.904
Movie" begs for repeat viewings.

00:06:12.119 --> 00:06:16.320
Prior to the release of the trailers, all
fans had to judge "The Super Mario Bros. Movie"

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.870
by was the film's official cast announcement,
which was revealed during a Nintendo Direct

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.750
presentation in September 2021.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.919
Among the most controversial of those reveals
was Chris Pratt as the voice Mario, replacing

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.910
the character's longtime voice actor Charles
Martinet.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.510
Fans were also divided over the announcements
of Charlie Day as Mario's brother Luigi, as

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.640
well as Seth Rogen as Donkey Kong.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.870
Many complained about the blanket decision
to cast Hollywood stars rather than professional

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:42.870
voice actors.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.560
Pratt said that he understood fans' concerns,
but urged,

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:49.160
"Go watch the movie and, and, and then we
can talk."

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:53.500
Even with some fans' hesitations about the
cast, it seems they turned up to the theater

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.230
to see for themselves, just like Pratt requested.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.889
While some critics felt that Pratt and Day
still weren't right for the characters, others

00:06:59.889 --> 00:07:03.910
felt they delivered with loyalty, originality,
and comedic chemistry.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:08.759
Even Kotaku noted the beauty of Martinet voicing
Mario and Luigi's dad in a moment that somewhat

00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:11.039
passes the torch to the two actors.

00:07:11.296 --> 00:07:15.700
While other voice actors have divided audiences,
Jack Black has been receiving nothing but

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:19.720
goodwill for portraying the film's antagonist
and scene-stealer, Bowser.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.120
Fans were excited by the announcement that
Black was joining the film, but they were

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:26.759
even more thrilled when the film's first trailer
showed that he brought his A-game to play

00:07:26.759 --> 00:07:28.669
the king of the Koopa army.

00:07:28.669 --> 00:07:32.220
But none of the previews truly captured Black's
fantastic performance.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.130
The trailers portrayed Bowser as a terrifying
threat to the Mushroom Kingdom, but in the

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:40.780
actual film it's revealed that Bowser is pining
for Princess Peach's hand in marriage, making

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.949
for some devastatingly funny moments.

00:07:42.949 --> 00:07:47.750
In one standout scene, Bowser sits at a piano
to sing an ode to Princess Peach, called "Peaches,"

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.750
and it's a brilliant use of Black's musical
talent.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:55.099
"Peaches" began to climb the iTunes charts
only a few days after the movie's release.

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:59.530
Black even stars in a music video for the
ballad, fully clad in Bowser-inspired garb.

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:00.980
It's a big screen showcase

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:05.009
Illumination has on occasion been criticized
for its storytelling, overuse of needle drops

00:08:05.009 --> 00:08:10.380
of popular songs, and low-brow humor, which
is never more present than in the "Despicable

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.380
Me" franchise.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.230
But the animation studio has always excelled
in its visuals, which often come to life more

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.090
brilliantly on a movie screen than they would
on smaller screens.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:21.500
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie," in this regard,
is no exception.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:26.180
If anything, this is a quality that Illumination
shares with Nintendo, which is often praised

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.160
for creating video games with colorful, vibrant
visuals and gameplay but lackluster stories

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:32.390
and narrative themes.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:36.000
Frankly, the film overdelivers when it comes
to its action sequences.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.525
These moments are as equally fluid in their
animation as they are overwhelming in a visual sense.

00:08:40.525 --> 00:08:42.820
Take, for instance, the film's Rainbow Road
scene.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.070
It offers an action-packed, "Mad Max: Fury
Road"-style battle between the Kong army and

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:51.670
Bowser's forces, while playing off tropes
and references from the "Mario Kart" franchise.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:56.290
Anya Taylor-Joy, who voices Peach, even drew
a comparison between this film and her upcoming

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.480
portrayal of Furiosa in the "Fury Road" prequel.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.450
"Bizarre that the two characters in my filmography
that have the most in common are Princess

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:04.950
Peach and Furiosa."

00:09:05.488 --> 00:09:10.628
Early reviews of "The Super Mario Bros. Movie"
weren't especially kind about its cinematic qualities.

00:09:10.628 --> 00:09:15.600
While some rightly appreciated the film as
a love letter to Nintendo's biggest franchise,

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.470
others were critical of the plot, soundtrack,
and humor.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.459
It was hovering around a 50% critic rating
on Rotten Tomatoes, though that has increased

00:09:23.459 --> 00:09:24.600
a bit since.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:29.551
Some critics even labeled "The Super Mario
Bros. Movie" as one of Illumination's worst offerings.

00:09:29.551 --> 00:09:33.540
That certainly came as quite the surprise
for hardcore "Super Mario Bros." fans, who

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:38.140
started worrying that Illumination would wash
out the franchise's most appealing qualities.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:42.149
But lots of moviegoers also seemed to ignore
the early criticism.

00:09:42.149 --> 00:09:46.310
Ultimately, fans had to be gratified that
Illumination did a good job faithfully adapting

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:51.240
their beloved franchise, especially compared
to the 1993 live-action film.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.149
While it may not be enough to woo folks who
are unfamiliar with the games, distrust of

00:09:55.149 --> 00:09:59.488
those early reviews convinced skeptical Nintendo
fans to check it out for themselves.

00:09:59.757 --> 00:10:04.519
Video game-inspired movies have had a rocky
past, making Nintendo hesitant to license

00:10:04.519 --> 00:10:09.320
their intellectual property to studios eager
to adapt the company's best-selling games.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.380
Longtime Nintendo game designer Shigeru Miyamoto,
who created Mario, told Variety,

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:17.220
"We were fearful of all the failure of past
IP adaptations."

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:22.115
Thankfully, the tide has turned lately thanks
to more faithful adaptations of many video games.

00:10:22.115 --> 00:10:26.519
One of those successes has been the live-action
"Sonic the Hedgehog" films starring Ben Schwartz

00:10:26.519 --> 00:10:28.710
as the voice of the titular blue blur.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.600
Early trailers concerned hardcore fans of
the series due to Sonic's design.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:36.440
This resulted in a last-minute delay so that
Paramount Pictures could redesign Sonic's

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.490
look to more closely resemble his appearance
in the games.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:44.764
Once the film debuted, audience response to
the movie and its 2022 sequel was extremely positive.

00:10:44.764 --> 00:10:49.070
Even more recently, HBO had a bona fide hit
on its hands with its adaptation of Naughty

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:53.680
Dog's "The Last of Us," which worried fans
who were devoted to the original game's actors.

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:58.190
Nevertheless, Pedro Pascal and Bella Ramsey
proved themselves to audiences, securing the

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:01.480
show a second season renewal only two weeks
into airing.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:07.530
By then, fans likely felt better about "The
Super Mario Bros. Movie" living up to expectations.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:12.899
Given the box office failure of the 1993 "Super
Mario Bros." film, Nintendo was much more

00:11:12.899 --> 00:11:17.660
hands-on in terms of making sure Illumination's
animated film would represent the company's

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.779
brand and be consistent with the Mario of
the games.

00:11:20.779 --> 00:11:26.519
As a result, Shigeru Miyamoto served as co-producer
of the film, alongside Meledandri, who welcomed

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:30.149
the input of one of the most influential figures
in video game history.

00:11:30.149 --> 00:11:31.880
Miyamoto told Rolling Stone,

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:36.089
"We started to want to focus on the idea of
wanting people to enjoy Nintendo and love

00:11:36.089 --> 00:11:40.420
Nintendo as Nintendo, not specifically as
any certain game."

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.260
That approach to a more holistic style of
branding resulted in a film collaboration

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:48.370
with Illumination, as well as the addition
of the Super Nintendo World theme park at

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:49.829
Universal Studios.

00:11:49.829 --> 00:11:54.060
It was important for Miyamoto, as a herald
of Nintendo's original spirit, to capture

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.800
that spirit outside the world of video games.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:01.231
Nintendo fans may have been worried that like
the 1993 film, Illumination's take on "Super

00:12:01.231 --> 00:12:05.110
Mario Bros." would substantially diverge from
the source material.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:10.919
But Nintendo was careful to make sure the
film didn't erase Mario's backstory or characterization.

00:12:11.267 --> 00:12:15.519
Of course, "The Super Mario Bros. Movie" wouldn't
be as adored by fans unless it featured some

00:12:15.519 --> 00:12:18.639
of the franchise's most iconic music tracks.

00:12:18.639 --> 00:12:23.170
Composer Brian Tyler helmed the film's score,
borrowing melodies and songs from Koji Kondo's

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:25.959
original music throughout the franchise's
history.

00:12:25.959 --> 00:12:30.410
This is mostly present in the film's many
action sequences, which use familiar themes

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.840
that will make any "Super Mario Bros." fan
squeal with excitement.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:39.167
Tyler described the process of adding Kondo's
original music to the film's soundtrack, telling Variety,

00:12:39.167 --> 00:12:42.620
"I wanted to have built-in nostalgia where
it immediately feels like Mario."

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:47.130
This even contributes to some Easter eggs
from the film, such as Luigi's ringtone being

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:52.339
the iconic GameCube jingle, or Bowser and
Kamek duetting on piano to play the World

00:12:52.339 --> 00:12:55.019
1-2 music from the original "Super Mario Bros."

00:12:55.019 --> 00:12:58.870
All that said, some fans found reasons to
criticize the soundtrack.

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:02.950
Along with oddly-placed pop songs during some
of the film's key moments, fans lamented the

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:07.910
lack of credit to composer Grant Kirkhope,
who wrote the infamous "DK Rap" that is featured

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.889
in Donkey Kong's introduction scene.

00:13:10.451 --> 00:13:15.170
One thing Nintendo found particularly appealing
about making "The Super Mario Bros. Movie"

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:19.460
was the notion that it not only appeals to
longtime fans, but also introduces the world

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.130
of the games to those who may not be familiar
with it.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:26.850
Former Nintendo of America president Reggie
Fils-Aime described the intent of the Illumination

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.529
partnership to IGN, saying,

00:13:28.529 --> 00:13:33.085
"It will be a great introduction to folks
who are not as familiar with the world of Mario."

00:13:33.085 --> 00:13:37.410
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" does a great
job of appealing to younger audiences, an

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.770
aspect that can also be applied to the "Super
Mario" video games.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:46.250
The games thrive off fun gameplay and lovable
characters rather than complex themes or controls.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:50.440
Although the film is certainly not for everyone,
many kids will likely walk out of the theater

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.100
desperate to play the latest entry in Nintendo's
franchise.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:58.160
Even nostalgic adults may find themselves
returning to their favorite childhood classics

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.040
after watching the Illumination movie.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.149
Either way, it wouldn't be surprising if the
film's box office success was a result of

00:14:04.149 --> 00:14:07.015
either of these groups going back for seconds.

00:14:07.015 --> 00:14:09.750
It's a good time to be an animation studio
in Hollywood.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.339
The past few years have seen a boom in original
animated films.

00:14:13.339 --> 00:14:17.579
Many film critics credit this surge to the
release of Sony's "Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse,"

00:14:17.579 --> 00:14:21.000
which wowed audiences with its comic-book-inspired
aesthetic.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.459
More films have profited off this mindset,
including Dreamworks' "Puss in Boots: The

00:14:25.459 --> 00:14:26.459
Last Wish."

00:14:26.459 --> 00:14:30.329
Like, "The Super Mario Bros. Movie," it was
a smash-hit at the box office despite the

00:14:30.329 --> 00:14:35.370
"Shrek" film franchise being dormant since
the last "Puss in Boots" film a decade ago.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:39.350
Audiences seem starved for animation that's
not only well-crafted, but contains more heart

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.940
and soul than other recent franchise films.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:47.200
The sentiment was even echoed during Guillermo
del Toro's acceptance speech at the 2023 Oscars.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:52.810
After winning Best Animated Film for his stop-motion
masterpiece, "Pinocchio," Del Toro championed

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:53.810
animation, saying,

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:58.780
"Animation is cinema, animation is not a genre,
and animation is ready to be taken to the

00:14:58.780 --> 00:14:59.780
next step."

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:06.197
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" may not innovate,
but it does satisfy audiences hungry for heartfelt animation.

00:15:06.197 --> 00:15:11.230
Nintendo is a true video-game giant, with
its many intellectual properties and dedication

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.280
to giving fans what they want.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:17.560
Nintendo is primed to continue its commitment
in film, with "The Super Mario Bros. Movie"

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:18.889
as just the start.

00:15:18.889 --> 00:15:23.160
Even before the film's release, both fans
and industry pundits alike were interested

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:26.149
in the possibility of a Nintendo Cinematic
Universe.

00:15:26.149 --> 00:15:29.880
This feeling was echoed by the film's cast,
who expressed their hopes for the franchise

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:30.960
to have a future.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.010
Although many film fans are growing tired
of never-ending cinematic universes, "The

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:38.329
Super Mario Bros. Movie" certainly promises
more from this world.

00:15:38.329 --> 00:15:42.720
A post-credits scene teases the introduction
of Yoshi, while other plot threads perfectly

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.420
set up a potential "Donkey Kong Country" spin-off.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.897
Even Charlie Day has indicated he'd be down
to reprise his role in a "Luigi's Mansion" movie.

00:15:49.897 --> 00:15:54.600
Illumination, for all its flaws, knows its
way around a franchise, and Nintendo's interest

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.970
in expanding its brand only makes this a greater
possibility.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:02.160
For Nintendo fans eager to see their favorite
characters on the big screen, seeing "The

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:07.010
Super Mario Bros. Movie" is not unlike Marvel
fans seeing the first "Iron Man" in 2008.

